IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g5-testing-bodies.l4: Chapter 5, Subchapter B of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025: ss.35 and 36 (the conditions to serve as a testing body; the
-- authorisation of testers and experts: the duty, the bar, the refusal, the conditions in the instrument, and the
-- period of the authorisation).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G5.  Imports only prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain.  Inputs: the Minister's
-- opinions and satisfaction, the Minister's judgement that circumstances make a person unfit, the further
-- conditions of a tender, the conditions of the regulations under s.60(1)(c) (not in the sources: a named
-- REFUSE unless the caller says), and the instrument of authorisation as the Minister wrote it.
--
-- A test the text lays down ("a corporation meeting all of these may serve as a testing body", "the Minister shall
-- not authorise a person who ...") is a BOOLEAN decision named for its section.  Duties are MUST rules, the bar
-- of s.36(b) is a SHANT rule, the refusal and the instrument powers of s.36(c), (d) are MAY rules.
--
-- Period met here: P23, the period for which an authorisation is granted, fixed by the Minister in the instrument
-- (s.36(e)); kind V (a period of validity), s.10(c) not applied (fork F-P23); the alternative is callable.

§ `Chapter 5, Subchapter B: testing bodies, and the authorisation of testers and experts`

§§ `Nouns of ss 35 and 36`

-- What s.35(2) and s.36(b)(1) ask about a person: convictions and pending proceedings, with the judgement that the
-- offence "by its nature, gravity or circumstances" makes him unfit.  Domain `Record of offences` carries the
-- facts; the judgement is an input.  `Record of offences` has an indictment field but no field for a criminal
-- proceeding on suspicion of an offence, so the broader reading (fork F-PROCEEDING) uses a field of its own,
-- requested as a noun in FRAGMENT-G5.md.
DECLARE `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` HAS
    `record of offences` IS A `Record of offences`
    `a conviction is for an offence that makes the person unfit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence suspected in a pending proceeding is one that would make the person unfit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a criminal investigation on suspicion of an offence is under way` IS A BOOLEAN   -- read only by the broader reading of "criminal proceeding"

-- The corporation, and each of its officers and controllers, as s.35(2) and (4) treat them.
DECLARE `Person connected with a testing body` HAS
    `standing as to offences` IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
    `may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN       -- s.35(4); the meaning is s.33 def.6

DECLARE `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` HAS
    `incorporated in Israel` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                  -- s.35(1)
    `registered in Israel` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                    -- s.35(1)
    `the corporation itself` IS A `Person connected with a testing body`
    `officers and controllers of the corporation` IS A LIST OF `Person connected with a testing body`
    `proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s.35(3)
    `the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement are met, if any were set` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN       -- s.35(5); NOTHING if none were set
    `already a testing body within section 33` IS A BOOLEAN                                               -- read only by the strict reading of s.35(3)

-- A person the Minister may authorise as a tester or an expert (s.36).
DECLARE `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` HAS
    `standing as to offences` IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
    `may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN                                -- s.36(b)(2)
    `meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c), if the caller says` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN   -- s.36(a); NOTHING: not said
    `the Minister found circumstances that make the person unfit to serve as a tester or an expert` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s.36(c)
    `the Minister gave the person his reasons for refusing` IS A BOOLEAN                                   -- s.36(c)
    `the person was given an opportunity to argue in writing` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- s.36(c)
    `the Minister refused to authorise the person` IS A BOOLEAN                                            -- s.36(c)

-- s.36(d): the two kinds of condition the Law names, "modes of action" and "work procedures".
DECLARE `Kind of condition or instruction under section 36(d)` IS ONE OF
    `a condition or instruction as to modes of action`
    `a condition or instruction as to work procedures`

DECLARE `Change under section 36(d)` HAS
    `kind` IS A `Kind of condition or instruction under section 36(d)`
    `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.36(e): the period the Minister fixes in the instrument, as he states it.
DECLARE `Period fixed in an instrument of authorisation` IS ONE OF
    `a number of days fixed in the instrument`    HAS `the number of days fixed` IS A NUMBER
    `a number of months fixed in the instrument`  HAS `the number of months fixed` IS A NUMBER
    `a number of years fixed in the instrument`   HAS `the number of years fixed` IS A NUMBER
    `a last day fixed in the instrument`          HAS `the last day fixed` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` HAS
    `granted on` IS A DATE
    `the period fixed in the instrument, if it fixes one` IS A MAYBE `Period fixed in an instrument of authorisation`

DECLARE `An act under sections 35 and 36` IS ONE OF
    `authorise a person as a tester or an expert`
    `refuse to authorise a person as a tester or an expert`
    `set conditions and instructions in the instrument of authorisation as to modes of action and work procedures`
    `change a condition or instruction in the instrument of authorisation`
        HAS `the change made` IS A `Change under section 36(d)`

§§ `Named refusals`

-- Each refusal is returned, never stored (a refusal nothing forces is no refusal); the name is the message.

-- s.60(1)(c), the regulations s.36(a) points at (line 448).
-- src:448 | {{ח:תתת|(ג)}} תנאים לשמש בודקים או מומחים לשם הסתייעות בהם לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 34|סעיף 34}}, ובכלל זה תנאים לעניין השכלה, ניסיון מקצועי, התמחות והכשרה; תקנות לפי פסקה זו טעונות התייעצות עם השר הנוגע בדבר בהתאם לתחומי עיסוקם של הבודקים או המומחים;

@ref s.36(a); s.60(1)(c) — regulations not in the sources (src:298, src:448)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no regulations under section 60(1)(c) are in the sources, and the caller has not said whether the person meets their conditions` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 60(1)(c) are in the sources, and the caller has not said whether the person meets their conditions"

@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the instrument of authorisation fixes no period, and s 36(e) gives no default` MEANS
    REFUSE "the instrument of authorisation fixes no period, and s 36(e) gives no default"

§§ `s 35 -- Conditions to serve as a testing body`

-- src:289 | {{ח:סעיף|35|תנאים לשמש גוף בודק}}
-- src:290 | {{ח:ת}} רשאי לשמש גוף בודק תאגיד שמתקיימים לגביו כל אלה:
-- s.35 lead-in: "a corporation meeting all of these may serve" is a passive eligibility test, not a permission
-- (phrasebook 5.1): a BOOLEAN decision.  The corporation, and each officer and controller, are `Person connected
-- with a testing body`.
-- src:291 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} הוא התאגד ונרשם בישראל;
@ref s.35(1) (src:291)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) — the corporation is incorporated and registered in Israel` corporation MEANS
        corporation's `incorporated in Israel`
    AND corporation's `registered in Israel`

-- src:292 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} הוא וכן נושא משרה או בעל שליטה בו לא הורשעו בעבירה שמפאת מהותה, חומרתה או נסיבותיה התאגיד אינו ראוי לשמש גוף בודק, ולא מתנהל נגדם הליך פלילי בשל חשד לביצוע עבירה כאמור;
-- s.35(2): "convicted of an offence that by its nature, gravity or circumstances makes the corporation unfit to
-- serve as a testing body", and no criminal proceeding is being conducted against them on suspicion of such an
-- offence.  The text does not say whose judgement "unfit" is (contrast s.36(b)(1): "in the Minister's opinion"):
-- an input, taken as the Minister's (fork F-JUDGE).  "Criminal proceeding" is read as a pending indictment (the
-- domain's field); the broader reading, which counts an investigation, follows (fork F-PROCEEDING).
@ref s.35(2) (src:292)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` standing MEANS
        (    standing's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a criminal offence`
         AND standing's `a conviction is for an offence that makes the person unfit` )
    OR  (    standing's `record of offences`'s `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet`
         AND standing's `the offence suspected in a pending proceeding is one that would make the person unfit` )

@ref s.35(2) (src:292)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding or investigation is pending on suspicion of one` standing MEANS
        (    standing's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a criminal offence`
         AND standing's `a conviction is for an offence that makes the person unfit` )
    OR  (    (    standing's `record of offences`'s `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet`
              OR  standing's `a criminal investigation on suspicion of an offence is under way` )
         AND standing's `the offence suspected in a pending proceeding is one that would make the person unfit` )

-- Fork F-OFFENCE: "offence" is bare in s.35(2), as in ss.30(b)(1) and 36(b)(1), where ss.6(a)(3), 21 and 23 say
-- "criminal offence" or "disciplinary offence".  Taken as a criminal offence; this counts a disciplinary conviction too.
@ref s.35(2) (src:292)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` standing MEANS
        (    (    standing's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a criminal offence`
              OR  standing's `record of offences`'s `convicted of a disciplinary offence` )
         AND standing's `a conviction is for an offence that makes the person unfit` )
    OR  (    standing's `record of offences`'s `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet`
         AND standing's `the offence suspected in a pending proceeding is one that would make the person unfit` )

@ref s.35(2) (src:292)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Person connected with a testing body`
`the corporation, its officers and its controllers` corporation MEANS
    (corporation's `the corporation itself`) FOLLOWED BY (corporation's `officers and controllers of the corporation`)

@ref s.35(2) (src:292)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` corporation MEANS
    all (GIVEN connected YIELD NOT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` (connected's `standing as to offences`))
        (`the corporation, its officers and its controllers` corporation)

@ref s.35(2) (src:292)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding or investigation` corporation MEANS
    all (GIVEN connected YIELD NOT `s 35(2), a criminal investigation counting as a proceeding — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding or investigation is pending on suspicion of one` (connected's `standing as to offences`))
        (`the corporation, its officers and its controllers` corporation)

-- src:293 | {{ח:תת|(3)}} הוא הוכיח, להנחת דעתו של השר, כי הוא מעסיק בודקים בתחומים ובהיקף הנדרשים לשם ביצוע בדיקות עזר ולשם עמידה בלוחות הזמנים לפי חוק זה;
-- s.35(3): the corporation "proved, to the Minister's satisfaction, that it employs testers in the fields and
-- scope required to carry out auxiliary tests and to meet the Law's deadlines".  The satisfaction is the
-- Minister's: an input.  A circularity sits here: "tester" (s.33 def.2) is an employee of a testing body, and a
-- testing body (def.4) must meet s.35(3) (fork F-LOOP, FRAGMENT-G5.md, contradictions).  Reading taken: "testers"
-- here are persons who hold the s.36 authorisation to test; the strict reading follows and can never be met.
@ref s.35(3) (src:293)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(3) — the corporation proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` corporation MEANS
    corporation's `proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required`

@ref s.35(3) (src:293)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(3), strictly — the corporation proved that it employs testers, a tester being an employee of a testing body` corporation MEANS
        corporation's `already a testing body within section 33`
    AND corporation's `proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required`

-- src:294 | {{ח:תת|(4)}} הוא וכן נושא משרה או בעל שליטה בו אינם עלולים להימצא, במישרין או בעקיפין, במצב של ניגוד עניינים;
-- s.35(4): neither the corporation nor an officer or controller "may be" (the wording of src:294) in a conflict of interest, directly
-- or indirectly.  The risk is a judgement and an input per person; the meaning of "conflict of interest" is
-- s.33 def.6, decided by g5-senior-inspector's `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest`.
@ref s.35(4) (src:294)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(4) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller may be in a conflict of interest` corporation MEANS
    all (GIVEN connected YIELD NOT connected's `may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly`)
        (`the corporation, its officers and its controllers` corporation)

-- src:295 | {{ח:תת|(5)}} תנאים נוספים, אם נקבעו במכרז או בתנאי ההתקשרות.
-- s.35(5): "further conditions, if set in the tender or in the terms of engagement".  The text names the absent
-- case itself ("if set"), so it is a MAYBE: none set means none to meet.
@ref s.35(5) (src:295)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(5) — the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement, if any, are met` corporation MEANS
    CONSIDER corporation's `the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement are met, if any were set`
    WHEN JUST met THEN met
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN TRUE

@ref s.35 (src:289-295)
@export Whether a corporation may serve as a testing body under s.35 of the Law: incorporated and registered in Israel; no disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding against it or an officer or controller; proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers; no conflict of interest likely; and any further conditions of the tender met
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` @desc The corporation, its officers and controllers with their records and conflict risks, the Minister's satisfaction, and the further conditions of the tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35 — the corporation may serve as a testing body` corporation MEANS
        "(1)" ... `s 35(1) — the corporation is incorporated and registered in Israel` corporation
    AND "(2)" ... `s 35(2) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller has a disqualifying conviction or pending proceeding` corporation
    AND "(3)" ... `s 35(3) — the corporation proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` corporation
    AND "(4)" ... `s 35(4) — neither the corporation nor an officer or controller may be in a conflict of interest` corporation
    AND "(5)" ... `s 35(5) — the further conditions set in the tender or the terms of engagement, if any, are met` corporation

§§ `s 36 -- Authorisation of testers and experts`

-- src:297 | {{ח:סעיף|36|הסמכת בודקים ומומחים}}
-- src:298 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} השר יסמיך בודקים ומומחים שמתקיימים לגביהם תנאים שקבע בתקנות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 60|סעיף 60(1)(ג)}}, לבצע בדיקות עזר או לתת חוות דעת מומחה, לפי העניין, לצורך הסתייעות בממצאיהן, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 34|בסעיף 34}}.
-- s.36(a): the conditions are "set by regulations under s.60(1)(c)", which are not in the sources (trap T31,
-- integration point IP14).  Whether a person meets them is a MAYBE the caller fills: JUST says it, NOTHING is a
-- named refusal, never FALSE.  The same words that govern s.30(a) and s.34(a) ("will authorise", the verb at src:298) read here
-- as a duty to authorise those who qualify: s.36(c) lets the Minister refuse "even if (a)'s conditions are
-- met", which presupposes that otherwise he must (fork F-DUTY).
@ref s.36(a) (src:298)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(a) — the person meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c)` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person's `meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c), if the caller says`
    WHEN JUST met THEN met
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `no regulations under section 60(1)(c) are in the sources, and the caller has not said whether the person meets their conditions`

-- src:299 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} לא יסמיך השר לבודק או למומחה מי שמתקיים לגביו אחד מאלה:
-- src:300 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הוא הורשע בעבירה שמפאת מהותה, חומרתה או נסיבותיה הוא אינו ראוי, לדעת השר, להיות מוסמך כאמור או שמתנהל נגדו הליך פלילי בשל חשד לביצוע עבירה כאמור;
-- src:301 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} הוא עלול להימצא, במישרין או בעקיפין, במצב של ניגוד עניינים.
-- s.36(b): the Minister shall not authorise a person who (1) was convicted of an offence that makes him unfit "in
-- the Minister's opinion", or against whom a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of such an offence, or
-- (2) may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly.
@ref s.36(b)(1) (src:300)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(b)(1) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` person MEANS
    `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` (person's `standing as to offences`)

@ref s.36(b)(2) (src:301)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(b)(2) — the person may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` person MEANS
    person's `may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly`

@ref s.36(b) (src:299-301)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` person MEANS
        "(1)" ... `s 36(b)(1) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` person
    OR  "(2)" ... `s 36(b)(2) — the person may be in a conflict of interest, directly or indirectly` person

-- The limbs run in this order so that a person barred by (b) is answered before the regulations (which the
-- sources do not contain) are asked: `FALSE AND r` does not force a refusal r.
@ref s.36(a), (b) (src:298-301)
@export Whether the Minister may authorise a person as a tester or an expert under s.36(a) and (b) of the Law: the person is not barred by a disqualifying conviction, a pending proceeding or a conflict of interest, and meets the conditions of the regulations under s.60(1)(c). Those regulations are not in the sources, so the answer is a refusal unless the caller states whether the person meets them
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert` @desc The person, with his record of offences and the Minister's opinions, his conflict risk, and, if the caller knows it, whether he meets the regulations' conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` person MEANS
        NOT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` person
    AND `s 36(a) — the person meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c)` person

-- src:302 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} השר רשאי לסרב להסמיך אדם לבודק או למומחה, אף אם מתקיימים לגביו התנאים כאמור בסעיף קטן (א), מנימוקים שימסור לו ולאחר שניתנה לו הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב, אם מצא כי קיימות נסיבות שבשלהן הוא אינו ראוי לשמש בודק או מומחה.
-- s.36(c): the Minister may refuse to authorise even a person who meets (a), "on reasons he gives him and after
-- he was given an opportunity to argue in writing", if he found circumstances that make him unfit.  A refusal
-- without the finding, the reasons or the hearing is not a refusal under (c): the guard refuses the act.
@ref s.36(c) (src:302)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` person MEANS
        "found circumstances" ... person's `the Minister found circumstances that make the person unfit to serve as a tester or an expert`
    AND "reasons" ... person's `the Minister gave the person his reasons for refusing`
    AND "hearing" ... person's `the person was given an opportunity to argue in writing`

@ref s.36(c) (src:302)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` person MEANS
        person's `the Minister refused to authorise the person`
    AND `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` person

-- The duty of s.36(a): the Minister must authorise the person unless s.36(b) bars him or he validly refused
-- under s.36(c).  No time is stated, so the duty carries no deadline.  The limbs run bar, refusal, regulations, so
-- that a person barred or validly refused is answered without asking the regulations, which the sources lack.
@ref s.36(a), (b), (c) (src:298-302)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` person MEANS
        NOT `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` person
    AND NOT `s 36(c) — the Minister validly refused to authorise the person` person
    AND `s 36(a) — the person meets the conditions set by regulations under section 60(1)(c)` person

@ref s.36(a) (src:298)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(a) — the Minister shall authorise the person as a tester or an expert` person MEANS
    IF   `s 36 — the Minister must authorise the person as a tester or an expert` person
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST  `authorise a person as a tester or an expert`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 36(a): a person who meets the conditions, is not barred and was not validly refused was not authorised"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Fork F-DUTY: read as a power, the Minister MAY authorise a person who may be authorised, and need not.
@ref s.36(a) (src:298)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise the person as a tester or an expert` person MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `authorise a person as a tester or an expert`
          PROVIDED `s 36 — the person may be authorised as a tester or an expert` person

@ref s.36(b) (src:299-301)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(b) — the Minister shall not authorise the person as a tester or an expert` person MEANS
    IF   `s 36(b) — the person is barred from authorisation` person
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         SHANT `authorise a person as a tester or an expert`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 36(b): a person with a disqualifying conviction, a pending proceeding or a conflict of interest was authorised"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.36(c) (src:302)
GIVEN person IS A `Person to be authorised as a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person as a tester or an expert` person MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `refuse to authorise a person as a tester or an expert`
          PROVIDED `s 36(c) — the Minister may refuse to authorise the person` person

-- src:303 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} השר רשאי להורות בכתב ההסמכה על תנאים והוראות לעניין דרכי פעולתו וסדרי עבודתו של בודק או של מומחה, ובכלל זה לפי סוגים של בדיקות עזר שהוא מוסמך לבצע, ורשאי הוא לשנות תנאים והוראות שנתן לעניין דרכי פעולתו לאחר שניתנה לבודק או למומחה הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב.
-- s.36(d): the Minister may set conditions and instructions in the instrument on modes of action and work
-- procedures, including by kind of auxiliary test.  Nothing conditions the power to set them.
@ref s.36(d) (src:303)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(d) — the Minister may set conditions and instructions in the instrument of authorisation` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `set conditions and instructions in the instrument of authorisation as to modes of action and work procedures`

-- The power to CHANGE, though, follows a written hearing, and its words cover only what he gave "as to modes of
-- action" (the words at src:303), where the power to set covers "modes of action and work procedures": reading A takes
-- the change power as narrower than the setting power; reading B covers both kinds (fork F-CHANGE).
@ref s.36(d) (src:303)
GIVEN change IS A `Change under section 36(d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(d) — the change concerns modes of action` change MEANS
    CONSIDER change's `kind`
    WHEN `a condition or instruction as to modes of action`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a condition or instruction as to work procedures` THEN FALSE

@ref s.36(d) (src:303)
GIVEN change IS A `Change under section 36(d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` change MEANS
        `s 36(d) — the change concerns modes of action` change
    AND change's `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing`

@ref s.36(d) (src:303)
GIVEN change IS A `Change under section 36(d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(d), reading B — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action or work procedures, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` change MEANS
    change's `the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing`

@ref s.36(d) (src:303)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(d) — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave as to modes of action, after a written hearing` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `change a condition or instruction in the instrument of authorisation` made
          PROVIDED `s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` made

@ref s.36(d) (src:303)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 35 and 36`
`s 36(d), reading B — the Minister may change a condition or instruction he gave, after a written hearing` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `change a condition or instruction in the instrument of authorisation` made
          PROVIDED `s 36(d), reading B — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action or work procedures, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` made

§§§ `s 36(e) -- the period of the authorisation (P23)`

-- src:304 | {{ח:תת|(ה)}} הסמכה לבודק או למומחה תהיה לתקופה שיורה השר בכתב ההסמכה.
-- s.36(e): "an authorisation to a tester or expert will be for the period the Minister directs in the instrument".
-- P23.  Kind X (the length is the Minister's, an input) and V (a period of validity).  The instrument states the
-- period as a number of days, months or years from the day it is granted, or as a last day; the end of a counted
-- period is Interpretation Law s.10(a) (days) or s.10(b) (months, years), from the module il-interpretation-time.
-- s.10(c) is NOT applied (kind V: the rule moves the end of a time for DOING something, and a period of validity
-- is not that; fork F-P23): the alternative applying it follows.  The day of the grant is a day of the
-- authorisation: s.10(a) leaves it out of the COUNT only.  An instrument that fixes no period is a named refusal.
@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
GIVEN granted IS A DATE
      period IS A `Period fixed in an instrument of authorisation`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 36(e) — the last day of a period fixed in an instrument granted on` granted period MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN `a number of days fixed in the instrument`   n THEN `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` granted
    WHEN `a number of months fixed in the instrument` n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `months from the day` granted
    WHEN `a number of years fixed in the instrument`  n THEN `s 10 — the last day of a period of` n `years from the day` granted
    WHEN `a last day fixed in the instrument` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
GIVEN granted IS A DATE
      period IS A `Period fixed in an instrument of authorisation`
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of a period fixed in an instrument granted on` granted period cal MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN `a number of days fixed in the instrument`   n THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `days from` granted `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of months fixed in the instrument` n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `months after an event on` granted `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a number of years fixed in the instrument`  n THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` n `years after an event on` granted `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (cal's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN `a last day fixed in the instrument` lastDay   THEN lastDay

@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
GIVEN instrument IS AN `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` instrument MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument's `the period fixed in the instrument, if it fixes one`
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN `the instrument of authorisation fixes no period, and s 36(e) gives no default`
    WHEN JUST period THEN `s 36(e) — the last day of a period fixed in an instrument granted on` (instrument's `granted on`) period

@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
GIVEN instrument IS AN `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)`
      cal IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the authorisation` instrument cal MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument's `the period fixed in the instrument, if it fixes one`
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN `the instrument of authorisation fixes no period, and s 36(e) gives no default`
    WHEN JUST period THEN `s 36(e), s 10(c) applied — the last day of a period fixed in an instrument granted on` (instrument's `granted on`) period cal

@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
@export Whether a day falls within the period of an authorisation of a tester or expert: from the day it was granted to the last day of the period the Minister fixed in the instrument (Law s.36(e)); a refusal if the instrument fixes no period. This does not account for revocation or suspension under s.39
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      instrument IS AN `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` @desc The day the authorisation was granted and the period the instrument fixes, if it fixes one
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` day `under` instrument MEANS
        day AT LEAST instrument's `granted on`
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (`s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` instrument)

-- Fork F-START: the alternative begins the authorisation the day AFTER it was granted.
@ref s.36(e) (src:304)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      instrument IS AN `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(e), beginning the day after the grant — the authorisation runs on the day` day `under` instrument MEANS
        day AT LEAST (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (instrument's `granted on`))
    AND `s 8 — the date` day `is up to and including` (`s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` instrument)
